  "notes": [
    "Offline simplification is a lossy CC0 adaptation, not a newly measured Naples tree. Existing OSM tree-node positions are not part of, or altered by, this research.",
    "Source branch UV1 and its exact used KHR_texture_transform are baked into UV0 before UV1 is removed. Leaf atlas UV0 and trunk UV0 are retained.",
    "Geometry-only uncompressed GLBs require no Draco, meshopt decoder, images or external runtime fetch. Bind existing bark/leaf PBR materials by the stable role names.",
    "The JPEG leaf diffuse has no alpha channel. Attach the unchanged separate PNG alpha through the existing Babylon material factory. No image pixels are edited or packed.",
    "Every original connected index component of the leaf primitive is retained. Bark primitives retain their recorded global simplification diagnostics. Component-local leaf simplification changes only triangle indices selecting original P/N/UV vertices; no leaf scale inflation, UV flip, image edit, Prune or Permissive is used. Components are not asserted to be individual leaves.",
    "Exact geometric area, summed absolute UV area, and 64-sample alpha-covered area are compared with the original before reduction. Net area and per-component clamped retention are recorded; bounds and voxel occupancy alone do not demonstrate canopy density. Reported simplifier error and these metrics are diagnostics, not a silhouette or perceptual-quality guarantee. Near/far render review with the actual alpha material is required before runtime approval.",
    "No claim of GTA-equivalent or photographic tree quality follows from triangle reduction alone."
